From d5e75576212364d783c5528b8d0a3422620986ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maksym Vasylchuk <max@buzztv.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:39:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] configure: link iconv through LTLIBICONV, not LIBICONV

AM_ICONV_LINK sets both: LIBICONV for a direct compiler invocation, and
LTLIBICONV for a libtool one. This is a libtool project -- src/Makefile.am
builds libzvbi.la and links it against $(LIBS) -- so putting LIBICONV in
LIBS hands libtool something it is entitled to rewrite.

Which it does, differently depending on its version. LIBICONV is the
absolute path of libiconv.so when the library lives outside the standard
search path, and while libtool 2.6.2 passes that straight through, 2.4.7
drops it from the final link line entirely. The build then fails with
undefined libiconv, libiconv_open and libiconv_close -- but only on hosts
with the older libtool, which is the kind of difference that survives
local testing and fails in CI.

LTLIBICONV is the form intended for exactly this: it is what gettext
documents for use with libtool, and both versions honour it.
---
 configure.ac | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 38fc288..5540b22 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -321,7 +321,7 @@ AM_ICONV_LINK
 if test "x$am_cv_func_iconv" != xyes; then
   AC_MSG_ERROR([iconv() not found])
 fi
-LIBS="$LIBS $LIBICONV"
+LIBS="$LIBS $LTLIBICONV"
 
 dnl
 dnl Check for png library.
-- 
2.55.0

